<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Menabe</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first great Sakalava kingdom of western Madagascar, whose Maroserana kings built power on cattle, warfare and the cult of royal relics.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Menabe was founded in the mid-17th century by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroserana-dynasty">Maroserana dynasty</a>, which moved north from the south-west into the plains between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mangoky-river">Mangoky</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsiribihina-river">Tsiribihina</a> rivers. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andriandahifotsy">Andriandahifotsy</a>, remembered as a great conqueror, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> defeated local rulers with firearms obtained from European traders.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> kingship was sacred: relics of dead kings (dady) were kept and honoured in shrines, and royal ancestor cults bound subjects to the dynasty. The economy was based on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, and slaves and cattle were traded with Europeans at the coast. Royal princes went north to found <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boina">Boina</a>, extending Sakalava power along the west coast.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 19th century the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom</a> took parts of Menabe, though much of the kingdom resisted. The French occupied it after 1895, and the last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toera">Toera</a>, was killed in 1897. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> royal rituals continue in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/menabe.jpg" alt="Menabe" width="320" height="582"><figcaption>Image: Jippijip · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madagascar-Menabe-2023.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Andriandahifotsy, Toera</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Malagasy religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy (Sakalava)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sakalava kingdom of Menabe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=menabe" aria-label="Menabe on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5873 2929 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Menabe lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6193 3185L6286 3134M6193 3185L6286 3134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6286 3134h0M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6193 3185h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6193 3185h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=menabe">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

